<PageTitle>WhoWeAre</PageTitle>
<div>
   
        <div>
        <div class="custom-card" style=" background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom,#ffffff,#ffffff,#f9f9f9)">
                <h2>
                    About GPA Caribbean
                </h2>
                <div>
                    <div>

                        <img src="/images/logomain.png" alt="Logo" style="max-width: 300px; height: 300px;" />
                    </div>

                </div>
                <p>
                    GPA Caribbean is a regional youth development and empowerment organisation dedicated to preparing the next generation of Caribbean leaders, innovators, entrepreneurs, and professionals. The organisation seeks to unlock the potential of Caribbean youth by providing transformative learning experiences, cross-border opportunities, professional development pathways, and entrepreneurship support that strengthen regional integration and economic participation.
                </p>
                <p>
                    GPA Caribbean operates on the belief that the Caribbean's greatest asset is its people, particularly its young population. By connecting youth across territories and creating opportunities for skills development, mobility, innovation, and leadership, the organisation contributes to a more competitive, connected, and prosperous Caribbean.
                </p>
           </div>
            <!-- Vision Statement Card -->
            <div class="custom-flex-row">
                <div class="custom-card" style="width:20rem; background-color: darkblue; color: white">
                    <h2> Our Vision</h2>
                    <p>
                        To create a globally competitive, innovative, and interconnected Caribbean youth community that drives sustainable economic growth, regional cooperation, and social transformation.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Vision Statement Card -->
                <div class="custom-card" style="width:20rem; background-color: lightyellow">
                    <h2> Our Mission</h2>
                    <p>
                        To empower Caribbean youth and nurture professional growth through transformative training, international exchange and travel opportunities, STEM-focused internships, entrepreneurship development, and leadership programmes that foster innovation, economic participation, and meaningful people-to-people integration across the Caribbean region.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
   
</div>

<div class="custom-card">
    <h1>
        Meet the Principal Officer
    </h1>
    <div>
        <img src="/images/logomain.png" alt="Logo" style="max-width: 300px; height: 300px;" />
    </div>
    <h3>Harry Logan – Principal Officer</h3 >
    <div style="height:1.25rem"></div>
    <p>
        Harry Logan began his professional career as Assistant Publicity Officer with the largest social work agency in the Caribbean. This role exposed him to the value of skills training and the importance of equipping young people with the life skills needed to navigate an increasingly complex world.
    </p>
    <p>
        During his early years of service, he travelled extensively throughout Jamaica, including some of the country's most remote communities. These experiences gave him firsthand insight into the transformative impact of youth camps, skills training programmes, and community cooperation on individual and community development.
    </p>
    <p>
        Mr. Logan played an integral role in the introduction of the Canada World Youth Exchange Programme, which paired local youth leaders with counterparts from Canada. Through this initiative, participants spent extended periods living and working in each other's communities while collaborating to address local challenges and support community development efforts.
    </p>
    <p>
        He later worked in disaster preparedness and management across the Caribbean, serving on the development communications team for the Pan Caribbean Disaster Preparedness and Prevention Project (PCDPPP) based in Antigua. He also contributed to the World Meteorological Organization's Flood Plain Mapping Project (FPMP) through Jamaica's Office of Disaster Preparedness and Emergency Management (ODPEM).
    </p>
    <p>
        Mr. Logan subsequently became Eastern Caribbean Director of Joyst Caribbean Student Services, headquartered in Trinidad and Tobago. In this capacity, he introduced the Work and Travel Programme, providing opportunities for summer employment in the United States, as well as the IAESTE STEM Internship Exchange Programme.
    </p>
    <p>
        He later became the first Customer Affairs Analyst at the Office of Utilities Regulation (OUR) in Jamaica. There, he was responsible for producing the quarterly and annual Quality of Service Assessment Reports, which have become widely recognized benchmarks for measuring customer service performance among Jamaica's public utility providers.
    </p>
    <p>
        Mr. Logan also served in middle management at the Tax Administration Jamaica (TAJ), where he spent many years as a tax administrator, contributing to the effective administration of the country's tax system.
    </p>
    <p>
        Youth development and regional integration remain close to his heart. He firmly believes that education, exposure, and lifelong learning are powerful tools that can change family circumstances and alter life trajectories for generations.
    </p>
    <p>
        Mr. Logan is an alumnus of the University of the West Indies, Mona, where he studied Integrated Communications. He also attended the Management Institute for National Development (MIND) and remains an avid observer of regional development and public policy across the Caribbean.
    </p>

</div>


